      "entries": [
        "The acolyte takes the stance of thousand ants, a style mimicking the distracting strikes of a swarm of tiny, vicious creatures. The acolyte can make thousand wounds unarmed attacks. These deal 1d12 piercing damage; are in the brawling group; and have the backstabber, forceful, and unarmed traits. While in this stance, if the acolyte successfully Trips a target, the target is flat-footed until the start of the target's next turn."
